          "source": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
          "citation": "Chapter 3 p.8"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "a",
      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "v-chord-convergence-target",
      "narrative": "Martino prescribes the V chord of the II-V cadence as the exact structural moment where the convergence system is to be deployed: 'It was at this final juncture (II-V) where my convergence system was conceived, noticing all the chord possibilities on the final 5th chord in the cadence.' The student's task is to approach the V chord with the full arsenal of 24 scale colors and their extracted chords. Chapter 3, p. 8.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
