          "citation": "Chapter 3 p.8"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "a",
      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "dom7",
      "function_role": "color-tone-requirement",
      "narrative": "Martino prescribes applying multiple distinct scale colors to a single dom7 chord -- not merely one scale per chord: 'This, from listening to John Coltrane, Yusef Lateef and others caused me to try using many different scale \"color\" types on one chord (7th).' The entire 24-scale system exists to supply this variety of approach to the dominant. Chapter 3, p. 8.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
