      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "a",
      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "resolution-target",
      "narrative": "The maj7 chord (FA7 and its extended forms FA79, FA679) is prescribed as the canonical resolution destination for the entire convergence system. Chapter 7 establishes: 'Bb7b5, C7+5, C7b5, Gb7b5 [resolve to] FA7.' FA79 and FA679 appear throughout Chapters 7-8 as the tonic arrival points toward which all tritone-related approach chords converge. The student's goal is always to make these resolution targets sound inevitable. Chapter 7, p. 58.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
          "citation": "Chapter 7 p.58"
        },
        {
          "source": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
          "citation": "Chapter 7 p.59"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "g",
      "granularity_name": "voice-leading"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "360-degree-convergence-center",
      "narrative": "Martino prescribes conceptualizing the maj7 tonal center as the target of a 360-degree bombardment by all 24 scales: 'You might call this system the astrological charting of a key center because the 360 degree circle is used & the key center lies at the middle which represents the person or key acted upon. You are bombarding this person, or in this case key center with 24 scales & their constituent chords.' The maj7 resolution is not a passive landing but the active destination of a systematic multi-scale approach. Chapter 5, p. 33.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
        {
          "source": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
          "citation": "Chapter 5 p.33"
        }
      ],
      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "a",
      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "maj7",
      "function_role": "scale-derived-approach-sequence",
      "narrative": "Martino prescribes a three-step sequence for approaching any maj7 resolution: (1) internalize the destination through cadential repetition ('brainwash your ear with the tonality with several cadences into the key'), (2) execute the approach scale while aurally projecting the resolution, (3) extract all constituent chords from the scale as additional convergent devices. The maj7 landing is prepared, not improvised from ignorance. Chapter 4, pp. 32-34.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
