      "provenance": "extracted",
      "granularity_level": "a",
      "granularity_name": "harmonic-family"
    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "dorian-mode-convergence",
      "narrative": "Martino prescribes the Dorian mode as a convergence scale targeting the min7 function within the II-V: 'This scale is simply a dorian mode of the F major scale. It contains C7, G-7, EX. This scale contains the E-Bb tritone which belong to the C7 & F#7 chords which lead to F major.' The G-7 (min7) chord is listed as one of the Dorian scale's extracted character chords. Chapter 6, p. 37.",
      "source_principle_ids": [
        "pat-martino:system-of-tonal-convergence:convergence-system"
      ],
      "source_work_id": "system-of-tonal-convergence",
      "references": [
